node(node02953,function,[],[comment='forest patches arbitrarily allocated for useage of households to collect NTFPs, timber, palmwine, palmnuts, and to hunt and fish. This allocation is necessary in order to allocate labour rationally, and to keep track of forest produce. The allocation is made to each of the five households in each lineage successively in the first five weeks of each year. Patches of all forest fallow and forest classes are allocated on the basis of a random window of patch size. This results in an unequal allocation of patches to households (between 6 and 20 patches are allocated to households in test runs) but the world is not equal anyway. A better method will hopefully be found later. The allocation is re-set each year, giving an artifical "holiday" at the end of the year, and a lag of up to five weeks before the highest number households can start working in the forest',name=fn7_0,units=int,value=(if-index(4)==week_decis&&forest_allocated==0&&patc_state>26&&patc_state<41&&patch_area>set_random&&patch_area<set_random+ 0.05 then hh_id_within_lineage else 0)],[]).
